 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T20:24+08:00",
 "answer": "**I’d have her skip the outdoor walk tomorrow morning, Sunday, October 18, and walk indoors instead.** Singapore’s forecast 24-hour PSI is **150–220 (Unhealthy to Very Unhealthy)**. At age 70, she is in a group more vulnerable to haze; Singapore’s Ministry of Health advises older adults to avoid outdoor activity when the **1-hour PM2.5** reading is in the High band. ([weather.gov.sg](https://www.weather.gov.sg/haze-situation-update-17-october-2026/))\n\nCheck the live **1-hour PM2.5** reading for your area in NEA’s myENV app before she goes out—the forecast and conditions can change. If she feels unwell or has heart or lung problems, be especially cautious and follow her doctor’s advice. ([weather.gov.sg](https://www.weather.gov.sg/haze-situation-update-17-october-2026/))",
